# Weekly Paid Media Report

## 1. Header — windows and completeness

| Item | Detail |
|---|---|
| Reporting window (last week) | **2026-10-24 → 2026-10-30** (7 days) |
| Comparison window (prior week) | **2026-10-17 → 2026-10-23** (7 days) |
| Context window (30-day) | **2026-10-01 → 2026-10-30** |
| **Data complete through** | **2026-10-30** — all 9 platform pulls returned `data_complete_through: 2026-10-30` |
| Anchor date | 2026-10-30 (`list_platforms`) |
| Source | Ad platforms only (`google_ads`, `meta_ads`, `reddit_ads`); spend, conversions, CPA are platform-reported |

**Known incompleteness:** none in the media data itself — both weekly windows are fully closed and complete through 2026-10-30. What is **absent by design** is anything post-conversion: no warehouse pipeline/leads data exists in this report (see Caveats).

## 2. Account summary (all platforms, platform-reported)

| Metric | Prior week (10-17→10-23) | Last week (10-24→10-30) | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $9,892.11 | $11,844.59 | +$1,952.48 (+19.7%) |
| Conversions | 53 | 65 | +12 (+22.6%) |
| Blended CPA | $186.64 | $182.22 | −$4.42 (−2.4%) |

*Sums of the three platforms' platform-reported totals below; blended CPA = spend ÷ conversions. Percentages computed from these absolute values.*

## 3. Per-platform detail

### Google Ads
| Metric | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $5,377.43 | $8,029.35 | +$2,651.92 (+49.3%) |
| Conversions | 28 | 42 | +14 (+50.0%) |
| CPA | $192.05 | $191.18 | −$0.87 (−0.5%) |

Driver: spend and conversions scaled together with CPA flat, which reads as a deliberate budget/pacing increase, not efficiency drift. (30-day context: $25,421.90 spend, 131 conversions, $191.06 CPA.)

### Meta Ads
| Metric | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $3,761.84 | $3,039.99 | −$721.85 (−19.2%) |
| Conversions | 19 | 16 | −3 (−15.8%) |
| CPA | $197.99 | $190.00 | −$7.99 (−4.0%) |

Driver: spend was cut and volume followed almost linearly; efficiency barely moved, so the cut bought ~$720 in savings at the cost of ~3 conversions. (30-day context: $15,109.76 spend, 79 conversions, $191.26 CPA.)

### Reddit Ads
| Metric | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $752.84 | $775.25 | +$22.41 (+3.0%) |
| Conversions | 6 | 7 | +1 (+16.7%) |
| CPA | $125.47 | $110.75 | −$14.72 (−11.7%) |

Driver: essentially flat spend with one extra conversion improved CPA; **at 6–7 conversions/week this is a single-conversion move and statistically noisy.** (30-day context: $3,210.19 spend, 26 conversions, $123.47 CPA.)

## 4. Recommendations (one per platform)

1. **Google Ads** — No budget change: CPA is flat (−0.5%) on the platform's largest spend increase (+49.3%). Recommended action: pull campaign-level detail to confirm what drove the spend ramp before any decision. Nothing filed.
2. **Meta Ads** — Filed pending proposal **`prop-aecb1061`**: restore weekly budget to $3,600 (from $3,039.99) as a one-week volume test.
3. **Reddit Ads** — Filed pending proposal **`prop-fcc2a673`**: increase weekly budget ~15% to ~$890 (from $775.25) as a signal-gathering test of the lowest CPA in the account.

## 5. Caveats

- **Data completeness:** both weekly windows are complete through 2026-10-30; no days are missing from the platform data.
- **Conversions are platform-reported only.** Conversion definitions differ per platform (source-of-truth wiki), so cross-platform conversion/CPA comparisons are directional, not apples-to-apples. A platform conversion is **not** a qualified lead.
- **No warehouse/pipeline data in this report.** My tools expose no leads, opportunities, or pipeline $, so no post-conversion outcome is quoted anywhere above.
- **Small volumes:** Reddit's 6–7 conversions/week makes its −11.7% CPA move low-confidence; even Google's +14 conversions is one week of data.
- **Attribution was not reconciled** across the three platforms; each figure is its own platform's count.
- **Recommendation status:** the two proposals are **pending human approval**; no change has been applied, scheduled, or confirmed.
